    "question": {
      ":question/id": "10e62df1-ae82-5616-887a-6033833d09b6",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $F$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\n- $H$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\n- $M$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${m}_{32}=1\\ne 0$.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ and $H$ are diagonal matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
